    ],
    "word_count": 50,
    "html": "<p>Karl Heckl was a Munich construction entrepreneur and civil engineer who served as president of TSV 1860 Munich from 1984 to 1988. He entered football administration as a millionaire from the building industry. Club delegates elected him president after he had initially said he would not stand for the presidency.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "As president of TSV 1860 Munich, Karl Heckl paid longstanding club debts and committed substantial personal funds to keeping the team competitive. He eventually offered a successor one million Deutschmarks to take over, presenting a cheque at a delegates’ meeting. No one accepted, and he remained for several more months.\n\nHis departure changed how the club assembled its side. Without his financial support, coach Willi Bierofka had a smaller budget and drew on the successful youth team. Seven young players, including Martin Spanring, joined the senior squad, which finished fifth in the Bayernliga.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 85,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Full eyewitness-based newspaper account and complete indexed club retrospective support funding decisions and the subsequent youth-based rebuild."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S3",
      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 93,
    "html": "<p>As president of TSV 1860 Munich, Karl Heckl paid longstanding club debts and committed substantial personal funds to keeping the team competitive. He eventually offered a successor one million Deutschmarks to take over, presenting a cheque at a delegates’ meeting. No one accepted, and he remained for several more months.</p>\r\n<p>His departure changed how the club assembled its side. Without his financial support, coach Willi Bierofka had a smaller budget and drew on the successful youth team. Seven young players, including Martin Spanring, joined the senior squad, which finished fifth in the Bayernliga.</p>\r\n"
  },
